{
  "title": "Tarsal Tunnel Syndrome",
  "url": "https://www.orthobullets.com/foot-and-ankle/7042/tarsal-tunnel-syndrome",
  "subtitle": "Updated: Jul 25 2025",
  "sections": [
    {
      "text": "Summary",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Tarsal Tunnel Syndrome is a compressive neuropathy of the tibial nerve at the level of the tarsal tunnel which can lead to pain and paresthesias of the plantar foot.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis can be suspected clinically with burning plantar foot pain with a positive Tinel's sign over the tibial nerve. EMG/NCS can help confirm the diagnosis.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Treatment is an initial trial of pain management and orthotics. Operative tarsal tunnel release is indicated in patients with persistent symptoms who fail nonoperative management.",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "-1",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Etiology",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "-1",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Mechanism",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "types of impingment",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "intrinsic",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "**ganglion cyst**",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tendonopathy",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "tenosynovitis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "lipoma/tumor",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "peri-neural fibrosis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "osteophytes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "extrinsic",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "shoes",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "trauma",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "anatomic deformity (tarsal coalition, valgus hindfoot)",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "post-surgical scaring",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "systemic inflammatory disease",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "edema of the lower extremity",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "cause of impingement able to be identified in 80% of cases",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Anatomy",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Posterior tarsal tunnel",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7042/images/tarsal-tunnel2.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "an anatomic structure defined by",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**flexor retinaculum** (laciniate ligament)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**calcaneus** (medial)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**talus** (medial)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "abductor hallucis (inferior)",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "contents include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**tibial nerve**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**posterior tibial artery**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**FHL tendon**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**FDL tendon**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**tibialis posterior tendon**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Tibial nerve",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "has 3 distal branches",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "medial plantar",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "lateral plantar",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "medial calcaneal",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "the medial and lateral plantar nerves can be compressed in their own sheath distal to tarsal tunnel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "bifurcation of nerves occurs proximal to tarsal tunnel in 5% of cases",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Anterior tarsal tunnel",
          "table": null,
          "images": [
            {
              "src": "https://upload.orthobullets.com/topic/7042/images/anterior_tibial_tunnel.jpg",
              "caption": ""
            }
          ],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "flattened space defined by",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "inferior extensor retinaculum",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "fascia overlying the talus and navicular",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "2",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "contents include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "2",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**deep peroneal nerve and branches**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**EHL**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**EDL**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**peroneus tertius**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "-1",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**dorsalis pedis artery**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Presentation",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "History",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may have previous trauma or surgery",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Symptoms",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "**pain**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "4",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**pain with prolonged standing or walking**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**often vague and misleading medial foot pain**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "**sharp, burning pains in the foot**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "numbness",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "intermittent paresthesias and numbness in the **plantar foot**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "may present as part of the \"heel pain triad\"",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "posterior tibial tendon deficiency (adult-acquired flatfoot), plantar fasciitis, tarsal tunnel syndrome",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "believed to be due to loss of static and dynamic stabilizers of the medial arch and susequent traction neuropathy on the tibial nerve",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "4",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Physical exam",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "tenderness of tibial nerve (tinel's sign)",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "sensory exam equivocal",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "pes planus",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "muscle wasting of foot intrinsics",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "abductor digiti quinti or abductor hallucis",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "pain with dorsiflexion and eversion of the ankle",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "compression test",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "plantar flexion and inversion of ankle",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "digital pressure over tarsal tunnel",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "highly senstitive and specific",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Imaging",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Radiographs",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "weight-bearing radiographs provide osseous structure",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "MRI",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "may be helpful to rule out **accessory muscle** or **soft-tissue tumor**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Studies",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "EMG",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "positive finding include",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "distal motor latencies of 7.0 msec or more",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": []
                },
                {
                  "text": "prolonged SENSORY latencies of more than 2.3 msec",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "sensory (SAP) more likely to be abnormal than motor",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "decreased amplitude of motor action potentials of",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "3",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "abductor hallucis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "or abductor digiti minimi",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "3",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Diagnosis",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "history is often most useful diagnostic aid",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "3",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Treatment",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Nonoperative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "lifestyle modifications, medications",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "usually ineffective",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "medications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "anti-inflammatory medications",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "SSRIs have been used",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "bracing",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "orthosis or foot wear changes to address alignment of hindfoot",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "can try a period of short-leg cast",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Operative",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "surgical release of tarsal tunnel",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "indications",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "after 3-6 months of failed conservative management and",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": [
                        {
                          "text": "compressive mass (ganglion cyst) identified",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "positive EMG",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        },
                        {
                          "text": "reproducible physical findings",
                          "table": null,
                          "images": [],
                          "importance": "2",
                          "children": []
                        }
                      ]
                    }
                  ]
                },
                {
                  "text": "outcomes",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "best results following surgery are in cases where a **compressing anatomic structure** (ganglion cyst) is identified and removed",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "traction neuritis does not respond as well to surgery",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "2",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Technique",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Tarsal Tunnel Surgical Release**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "5",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "approach",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "identify the nerve proximally",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "1",
                  "children": []
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "text": "decompression",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": [
                {
                  "text": "**layers that must be released include**",
                  "table": null,
                  "images": [],
                  "importance": "5",
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "text": "flexor retinaculum",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "deep investing fascia of lower leg",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    },
                    {
                      "text": "superficial and deep fascia of abductor hallucis",
                      "table": null,
                      "images": [],
                      "importance": "5",
                      "children": []
                    }
                  ]
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Complications",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "**Recurrence**",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "1",
          "children": [
            {
              "text": "usually caused by **inadequate release**",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "5",
              "children": []
            },
            {
              "text": "repeat tarsal tunnel release not recommended",
              "table": null,
              "images": [],
              "importance": "1",
              "children": []
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "text": "Prognosis",
      "table": null,
      "images": [],
      "importance": "3",
      "children": [
        {
          "text": "Results vary between 50-90% success",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Worse results with **'double crush'** injuries and post-operative scarring",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "4",
          "children": []
        },
        {
          "text": "Revision surgery less successful than index operation",
          "table": null,
          "images": [],
          "importance": "3",
          "children": []
        }
      ]
    }
  ],
